        "original_id": "9317e5d4-edf8-590f-9747-4f2fe95212dc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gül Mosque, Hippodrome of Constantinople, Istanbul, Turkey, Sultanahmet Meydanı\n- Organizations: Eastern Orthodox Church, Ottomans\n- Concepts: mosque conversion, historic square\n\nFacts:\n- Gül Mosque is in Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Gül Mosque is a former Eastern Orthodox church.\n- Gül Mosque was converted into a mosque by the Ottomans.\n- Gül Mosque is called \"Gül Camii\" in Turkish, meaning \"The Mosque of the Rose\" in English.\n- The former Hippodrome of Constantinople is today a square in Istanbul, Turkey.\n- The square on the site of the Hippodrome of Constantinople is named Sultanahmet Meydanı, meaning \"Sultan Ahmet Square.\"\n- A few fragments of the original Hippodrome of Constantinople structure still survive.",
